# death_if_fails rescaled for real per-act risk (drafts/repeats/rescale_death.py)
# Chroma library, modern Earth: RISK, DRUGS, THE HOSPITAL AND DYING BEFORE ONE'S TIME (next batch, Emren's point 11:
# "is it possible for character to wake up in hospital ... drugs ... Can character die before biological terminance?").
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: library-spec.md, drafts/next2/BRIEF.md. Ten everyday moments, each calling two colors,
# in two blocks of five whose calls go round all five colors twice (juvenile and young adult: WG WU UB BR RG; young adult
# and adult: WB BG UG UR WR), so every stage is called evenly; five life events (pairs D2a and D2b, triads of D4a and D4b,
# cross cycle s2) and one echo. Cross cycles s1 to s4 three times each.
# death_if_fails (engine 21:06): the share of an act's failures that end the character's life; never on an act under 12.
# No recipes, doses or method detail; nothing graphic; suicide and self-harm are never options.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: a vape behind the sports hall (calls WG, cycle s1)

== a vape passed round behind the sports hall
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 12-19
calls: WG
tone: mixed
life: friends, body
horizon: moment
roles: friend, rival, grandparent, a teacher
earth: at break, behind the sports hall, a sweet-smelling vape is going from hand to hand, and now it is your turn
times: Most teenagers are offered one, a few times in secondary school (estimate); about 1 in 5 of 11 to 17 year-olds in Great Britain have tried vaping (ASH 2024)
gap: 2-4
scene: Behind the sports hall the air smells of mango sweets. A vape is going from hand to hand, and now {friend} holds it out to {N}.
scene W: Everyone in the circle has had a go, and {N} is the only one left. The rule is not written anywhere, but everyone knows it.
scene U: {N} has read that these things hook people faster than cigarettes ever did, and is curious all the same what the fuss is about.
scene B: The ones passing it round are the ones everyone wants to sit with at lunch. A place in this circle is worth something.
scene R: The bell goes in four minutes, a teacher could turn the corner at any second, and {Ns} heart is going fast.
scene G: {grandparent} smoked all their life and coughed every morning {N} can remember. The sweet cloud drifts past as if it has nothing to do with that.
- W | take one pull, the way everyone in the circle has, and pass it on | habit | v: conformity | self_control: - | closed: approval: vaping at school; backfire: caught, and a letter home | norm: tobacco | chance: 90
- U | try the one with something stronger in it, just to see what it does | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: used drugs | body: light | closed: law: an illegal drug; backfire: sick and shaking in the toilets, and the school rings home | law: drugs | chance: 74
- B | buy your own from the older kid who sells them, and make sure everyone sees | v: power, achievement | closed: law: under age to buy; backfire: confiscated, and a letter home | chance: 68
- R | blow the biggest cloud anyone has seen, and wait for the cheer | habit | v: stimulation, hedonism | body: light | closed: approval: vaping at school; backfire: a coughing fit, and a teacher round the corner | norm: tobacco | chance: 84
- G | say no, thinking of your grandparent's cough, and stay in the circle anyway | identity | v: security, tradition | self_control: + | chance: 76
- W>U | ask the school nurse straight out what vaping does to a body | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- U>B | pretend to inhale, so you look like one of them without getting hooked | v: power, security | chance: 84
- B>R | swipe the vape from a bag when nobody is looking, and try it alone later | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 90
- R>G | drag your best friend off to kick a ball about instead, the way you used to | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 76
- G>W | tell your grandparent everything, and let them have a word with the school | v: security, tradition | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: telling on the circle; backfire: everyone guesses who told | chance: 80
works: The bell goes, and {N} walks back in still part of the group, and still themselves.
works: Nobody makes a thing of it, and by the end of the week {N} knows where they stand.
fails: A teacher turns the corner, and every name in the circle goes in the book.
fails: {N} coughs until their eyes stream, and the whole group laughs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: a drinking game (calls WU, cycle s4)

== a drinking game round the kitchen table
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 17-25
calls: WU
tone: mixed
life: friends, study
horizon: moment
roles: friend, rival, strangers, the neighbours
earth: the first week in halls or a new flat: twelve near-strangers round a kitchen table, a deck of cards and a drinking game with rules
times: Most young people who go to college or share a flat, several times in their late teens and early twenties (estimate)
gap: 2-4
scene: A new term, a new flat: twelve near-strangers sit round a sticky kitchen table with a deck of cards, and the game has rules {N} is still learning.
scene W: Break a rule, drink: everyone at the table plays by the same ones, and {N} wants to belong here.
scene U: {N} has spotted how the scoring works: whoever deals hardly drinks at all.
scene B: Whoever wins tonight will be the name everyone knows by Friday. {rival} from the floor above clearly wants it to be them.
scene R: Cards slap on the table, everyone is shouting, and the next round is a race.
scene G: These people will be {Ns} neighbours for a year, maybe friends for life. Somewhere round this noisy table, a household is forming.
- W | play strictly by the rules, and drink whatever the cards say | habit | v: conformity | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.002 | self_control: - | chance: 76
- U | fill your cup with water when nobody is looking, and play along | habit | v: security | chance: 84
- B | rig the deck so your rival loses every round | v: power, achievement | chance: 66
- R | take the forfeit nobody else will: the rest of the bottle, in one go | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | chance: 72
- G | slip out to the back step and talk with the quiet one who left early | v: benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 72
- W>G | suggest a rule that anyone may sit a round out, so everyone stays in the game | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 74
- U>W | keep a quiet tally of every player's drinks, and call time on anyone past it | v: security, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 66
- B>U | use the game's truth forfeits to find out everyone's secrets | v: power | chance: 82
- R>B | take your rival on head to head, loser drinks double | v: power, stimulation | body: heavy | chance: 76
- G>R | fetch the old guitar and turn the game into a singalong | v: hedonism, tradition | chance: 76
works: The kitchen becomes a household that night, and {N} is part of it.
works: {N} wakes clear-headed enough for the first lecture, with a dozen new numbers in the phone.
fails: {N} spends the night on the bathroom floor, and by morning everyone has heard about it.
fails: The game turns sour, a glass breaks, and the neighbours start banging on the wall.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: pills at a party (calls UB, cycle s4)

== a bag of pills in the party kitchen
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 15-25
calls: UB
tone: mixed
life: friends, body
horizon: moment
roles: friend, the host, a stranger
earth: in the kitchen at a party, someone you half know opens a little bag of pills and offers them round
times: About 1 in 3 young people, once or twice (estimate); a few in 100 of 16 to 24 year-olds in England and Wales take ecstasy in a year (ONS crime survey)
gap: 3-6
share: .33
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: In the crowded kitchen, a lad {N} half knows opens a little bag of pills and holds it out. "Go on. Everyone's having one."
scene W: {N} heard the warnings in assembly, and the host's parents trusted everyone tonight. {friend} is watching to see what {N} will do.
scene U: Nobody here knows what is in those pills, not even the one handing them out. {N} cannot stop thinking about that, and about wanting to know.
scene B: The seller is making a lot of money tonight, and he has a friendly eye on {N}. A favour now might be worth something later.
scene R: The music has just kicked up, the whole room is jumping, and {N} wants the night to go up a level.
scene G: Out of the window the garden is dark and still. The party feels like weather building, and {N} cannot tell yet which way it will turn.
- W | take one alongside your friend, so they are not in it alone | v: benevolence | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.003 | closed: law: illegal drugs; backfire: a bad night in hospital, or the police | self_control: - | law: drugs | chance: 74
- U | refuse anything nobody can say what is in | identity | v: security, self-direction | self_control: + | chance: 92
- B | keep the seller sweet, and save his number for later | v: power, security | chance: 70
- R | take one and dance | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.003 | closed: law: illegal drugs; backfire: a bad night in hospital, or the police | law: drugs | chance: 80
- G | take one out in the dark garden, under the trees, away from the crush | v: hedonism, universalism (nature) | self_control: - | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.003 | closed: law: illegal drugs; backfire: a bad night in hospital, or the police | law: drugs | chance: 76
- W>G | find the host and quietly tell them what is going round their parents' house | v: security, benevolence | closed: approval: telling on the seller; backfire: the seller's friends find out who told | chance: 78
- U>W | look up the markings on the pill, and warn everyone if they are bad | v: security, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | tech: internet | chance: 60
- B>U | flatter the seller into a free one, and see what it does | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.003 | closed: law: illegal drugs; backfire: a bad night in hospital, or the police | law: drugs | chance: 80
- R>B | grab the bag off the seller and pocket the lot | v: power, stimulation | mark: broke the law | body: light | closed: law: possession, and theft from a dealer; backfire: the seller's friends come looking | chance: 70
- G>R | skip the pills, and dance barefoot on the lawn until the sky gets light | v: hedonism | chance: 72
works: The night burns bright and then burns out, and {N} gets home as the birds start.
works: Nothing goes wrong, and by Monday the party is just a story.
fails: Someone collapses by the back door, and the party ends with an ambulance and a lot of parents.
fails: {N} spends the small hours sick and frightened in the bathroom, with {friend} knocking on the door.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: a dare on the factory roof (calls BR, cycle s3)

== a dare on the factory roof
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 13-21
calls: BR
tone: mixed
life: friends, risk
horizon: moment
roles: friend, rival, parent, a security guard
earth: at night on the roof of the empty factory, the dare is to jump the gap to the next roof
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 6 teenagers, mostly boys, once or twice (estimate); teenagers take far more risks with friends watching (Gardner and Steinberg 2005)
gap: 3-8
share: .17
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: It is dark on the roof of the empty factory. Between this roof and the next is a gap of two long strides above a three-storey drop, and {rival} has just jumped it.
scene W: {N} promised {parent} to stay away from the old factory, and this is very much inside it. Someone has to think about getting everybody down.
scene U: {N} measures the gap by eye: the run-up, the distance, and whether the far edge is solid or rotten.
scene B: {rival} cleared it and is grinning across the gap. If {N} does not jump now, everyone will be talking about it on Monday.
scene R: The town lights are spread out below, the wind is cold, and {Ns} legs are already itching to run.
scene G: Pigeons shift in the rafters below. The old building creaks as if it has had enough of people climbing on it.
- W | refuse, and talk the others into climbing down the way you came | v: security, benevolence | chance: 60
- U | walk the edge until you find the narrowest point, and jump there | v: achievement | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.01 | closed: law: trespass; backfire: the police, and a caution | chance: 80
- B | jump it filming on your phone, and post it for the views | identity | v: power, achievement | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.01 | closed: law: trespass, and the video is the proof; backfire: the police see it too | tech: phone | chance: 78
- R | take a run at it and jump | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.01 | closed: law: trespass; backfire: the police, and a caution | chance: 75
- G | sit with your back to the chimney, watch the lights, and let them jump | v: security, universalism (nature) | chance: 82
- W>R | agree on one jump each, in turn, then everyone off the roof together | v: conformity, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.01 | closed: law: trespass; backfire: the police, and a caution | self_control: - | chance: 84
- U>G | point out the rotten roofing, and explain why the far edge will not hold | v: universalism, security | chance: 64
- B>W | threaten to tell everyone's parents unless they all climb down now | v: security, power | chance: 66
- R>U | shout down into the empty hall below, and listen to how far the echo goes | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 70
- G>B | wait for the gusts to drop, then jump when your body says now | v: achievement | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.01 | closed: law: trespass; backfire: the police, and a caution | chance: 62
works: Everyone gets down in one piece, and the night turns into a story they will tell for years.
works: {N} gets home before midnight, shaking a little, and nobody at home suspects a thing.
fails: Someone lands badly on the far roof, and the night ends with an ambulance at the factory gate.
fails: A security guard's torch finds them, and the police drive {N} home.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: a joint at a friend's (calls RG, cycle s2)

== a joint going round at a friend's
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 14-25
calls: RG
tone: mixed
life: friends, body
horizon: moment
roles: friend, parent, the friend's older cousin
earth: on a friend's bedroom floor, with the window open and the music low, a joint is going round the circle
times: Most young people, a few times in their teens and twenties (estimate); 17 in 100 US high-schoolers used cannabis in the past month (CDC YRBS 2023)
gap: 2-4
scene: The window is open, the music is low, and a joint is making its way round the circle on {friend}'s bedroom floor.
scene W: {friend}'s parents are downstairs watching television, and {N} knows exactly what they would say. It is still against the law here.
scene U: {N} has read three different things about what this does to a young brain, and none of them agree. Here is a chance to find out first-hand.
scene B: {friend}'s older cousin brought it, and the cousin knows people. Being easy about this could open doors.
scene R: Everyone is laughing at nothing, the song is perfect, and the joint is two people away.
scene G: Nobody is in a hurry. The talk drifts, the smoke drifts out of the window, and the evening feels as if it could go on for ever.
- W | pass it on untouched, and say plainly that you would rather not | identity | v: conformity, security | self_control: + | chance: 82
- U | take one small pull, and pay close attention to what it does | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: used drugs | body: light | closed: law: cannabis is illegal here; backfire: hours of racing thoughts, or caught | law: drugs | chance: 76
- B | ask the cousin where it comes from, and whether there is money in it | door | v: power, achievement | chance: 66
- R | smoke every time it comes round, and laugh until your ribs hurt | habit | v: hedonism | mark: used drugs | body: light | closed: law: cannabis is illegal here; backfire: sick on the bathroom floor, and found out at home | self_control: - | law: drugs | chance: 78
- G | take your turn when it reaches you, slowly, and let the talk drift | habit | v: hedonism | mark: used drugs | body: light | closed: law: cannabis is illegal here; backfire: the smell goes home on every coat | law: drugs | chance: 80
- W>B | promise to say nothing to anyone's parents, and keep note of who owes the favour | v: power | chance: 78
- U>R | put on the album you have been saving, and turn it into a listening party | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 80
- B>G | leave early with an excuse about your sibling, and keep out of it | v: security | self_control: + | chance: 92
- R>W | snap at the others when they push the youngest in the room to try it | v: benevolence | mark: made an enemy | chance: 80
- G>U | go out into the garden alone and think about what you actually want | v: self-direction | chance: 80
works: The evening ends easy, and {N} cycles home with the night air on their face.
works: Nothing bad comes of it, and {N} knows a little more about the people in that room.
fails: {friend}'s mother opens the door, and the smell tells her everything.
fails: {N} goes quiet and strange inside, and the walk home is a long one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: cocaine at the office party (calls WB, cycle s3)

# gate: a career held (it is the firm's own party); left without needs: so the block's calls stay even for everyone
== cocaine at the office party
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: young_adult adult
age: 22-45
calls: WB
tone: mixed
life: work, leisure, body
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, boss, partner
earth: late at the office's year-end party, a senior colleague nods you towards the toilets and offers cocaine
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 10 office workers, once or twice, more in some trades (estimate); about 2 to 3 in 100 adults in England and Wales use cocaine in a year (ONS)
gap: 6-12
share: .1
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: It is late at the office's year-end party. {colleague} catches {Ns} eye, taps the side of their nose and nods towards the toilets.
scene W: {N} signed the firm's code of conduct in the first week, and it says plainly what happens to anyone caught with drugs.
scene U: {N} notices who comes back from the toilets talking too fast, and starts to see who belongs to which circle.
scene B: {colleague} is close to {boss}, and the inner circle seems to form in that corridor. Saying yes would mean being one of them.
scene R: The music is loud, the bar is free, and the night is nowhere near ready to end.
scene G: These are the people {N} sees every working day. Tonight they look like strangers wearing their faces.
- W | say a polite no, and stay in the main room until the taxis | v: conformity, security | chance: 82
- U | decline, and watch with interest how the evening changes everyone | v: self-direction | chance: 86
- B | go with them, because that corridor is where the real decisions get made | habit | v: power, achievement | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.002 | closed: law: illegal drugs, and a sacking offence; backfire: seen by the wrong person, and a disciplinary | law: drugs | chance: 80
- R | grab the microphone and start the karaoke, so the party stays out here | v: hedonism | chance: 80
- G | step outside into the cold and ring someone you love | v: benevolence, security | chance: 86
- W>R | join in once, because this team does everything together | v: conformity, hedonism | self_control: - | mark: used drugs | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.002 | closed: law: illegal drugs, and a sacking offence; backfire: seen by the wrong person, and a disciplinary | law: drugs | chance: 76
- U>G | say no with a reason everyone accepts: you are training for a marathon | v: security | chance: 72
- B>W | threaten to report your colleague unless they stop offering it to the juniors | v: security, power | chance: 76
- R>U | ask your colleague straight out why they need it to have fun | door | v: self-direction | chance: 76
- G>B | let the night run its course, and be the clear-eyed one at the nine o'clock meeting | v: achievement | chance: 70
works: Monday comes, and {N} walks into the office on easy terms with everyone.
works: The party ends at two, and {N} gets home with nothing to regret by morning.
fails: {N} spends Sunday with a racing heart and a dread that will not lift.
fails: Someone saw, and by Monday it has reached {boss}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday: a swim past the buoys (calls BG, cycle s3)

== a race to the rocks across the bay
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult
age: 16-45
calls: BG
tone: mixed
life: leisure, body, nature
horizon: moment
roles: friend, partner, a lifeguard
earth: on a hot afternoon, friends dare each other to swim to the rocks across the bay, past the buoys and the warning flags
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 6 people, mostly young men, once or twice (estimate); most people who drown in UK waters are men (National Water Safety Forum)
gap: 6-12
share: .17
rate: .5
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: It is a hot afternoon at the beach. {friend} points at the rocks across the bay, far beyond the buoys, and says the last one there buys the drinks.
scene W: The lifeguard has the warning flags up, and the sign says the current turns at this time of day. {N} has never once ignored a lifeguard.
scene U: {N} watches the water. A calm, darker lane runs straight out from the shore where the waves do not break, and {N} knows what that means.
scene B: {friend} has won every race this summer. {N} swims better than anyone thinks and would love to prove it.
scene R: The sea is glittering, the sun is hot on {Ns} shoulders, and the cold water is calling.
scene G: The tide is on the turn; {N} can feel it in the way the waves have changed. The sea has a mind of its own this afternoon.
- W | stay between the flags, and swim there while the others go | v: conformity, security | chance: 82
- U | swim well clear of the dark lane, and turn back at the first buoy | v: security, achievement | body: light | chance: 88
- B | stay on the sand holding the bets, and keep the winnings | v: power | chance: 84
- R | sprint into the waves and race them to the rocks | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.005 | closed: approval: swimming outside the flags; backfire: the lifeguard's whistle, and a dressing-down | chance: 70
- G | float on your back in the shallows, and let the tide decide | v: hedonism, universalism (nature) | chance: 90
- W>R | borrow a float from the lifeguard hut without asking, and swim out with them | v: stimulation, security | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | closed: approval: taking the lifeguard's float; backfire: a dressing-down in front of the whole beach | self_control: - | chance: 70
- U>G | explain the dark lane of water, and why today the sea is not for racing | v: universalism, benevolence | chance: 64
- B>W | offer to buy everyone's drinks if they all stay in the shallows | v: security, benevolence | chance: 68
- R>U | swim to the first buoy and back against the clock, to see how fast you are | habit | v: achievement, stimulation | body: light | self_control: + | chance: 80
- G>B | wait for the tide to turn, then win the race with it at your back | v: achievement | mark: took a wild risk | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.003 | closed: approval: swimming outside the flags; backfire: the lifeguard's whistle, and a dressing-down | chance: 62
works: Everyone is back on the sand by teatime, salty, sunburnt and laughing.
works: {N} comes out of the sea tingling all over, and the evening tastes better for it.
fails: The current takes someone out past the rocks, and the lifeguard's boat goes roaring after them.
fails: {N} swallows half the bay, and staggers out coughing and frightened.

