# ---------------------------------------------------------------- echo: waking up in hospital (cycle s1)

== waking up in hospital
tier: echo
at: hospital
stages: juvenile+
age: 12-110
after: mark 'used drugs' or 'took a wild risk' on an act that failed (an overdose, a crash, a fall, a night that went wrong)
delay: 0-1
likelier: a heavy act (body: heavy) or one with death_if_fails; a failure far from help
rarer: friends who stayed sober and called for help early; a light act
tone: trouble
life: body, health
horizon: week
roles: friend, parent, partner, a nurse, a doctor, the police
earth: you wake up in a hospital bed with a drip in your arm, and slowly the night comes back to you
times: Follows some failed risks: perhaps 1 in 4 nights that go badly wrong (an overdose, a crash, a fall) end in a hospital bed (estimate)
scene: {N} wakes under strip lights with a drip in one arm and a plastic band on the wrist. Slowly, in pieces, it comes back: what happened, and how it went wrong.
scene W: A nurse is going through a form at the end of the bed, asking the questions in order. {N} knows there are rules for what happens next, and honest answers are part of them.
scene U: {N} reads the chart clipped to the bed before anyone comes, trying to work out what happened and how bad it was.
scene B: {N} is already working out the story: what to say, to whom, and what nobody needs to know.
scene R: {Ns} whole body aches, and the first feeling, before fear or shame, is a fierce, odd gladness to be alive.
scene G: {friend} is asleep in the chair beside the bed, still in a coat, and must have been there all night.
