- U | read your own notes on the desk while nobody is looking | v: self-direction | closed: approval: reading files not meant for patients; backfire: a nurse catches it, and the doctors turn guarded | chance: 78
- B | get the story straight before anyone else talks, and tell it first | v: security, power | chance: 72
- R | pull out the drip and discharge yourself the moment you can stand | v: self-direction, stimulation | body: heavy | chance: 68
- G | let the family close ranks round the bed, and answer nobody's questions | v: security, tradition | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: shutting out the people who need answers; backfire: the questions come back harder | chance: 76
- W>U | sign up for the course the hospital offers people who come in this way | habit | door | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- U>B | find out what anyone actually knows before saying a word | v: security, power | chance: 72
- B>R | laugh it off with everyone, and start planning the next time | v: hedonism, stimulation | self_control: - | chance: 78
- R>G | cry when the family walks in, and let them see how scared you were | v: benevolence, security | chance: 82
- G>W | make a quiet vow at the bedside to change how you live | binds | v: tradition, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 74
works: The doctors let {N} go home after two days, with a leaflet, a bruise and a great deal to think about.
works: {N} walks out of the hospital into a bright, cold morning and breathes it in.
fails: The doctor's face is serious: there is damage that will take months to heal.
